<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Journals on Amal Chandran M V</title><link>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/</link><description>Recent content in Journals on Amal Chandran M V</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 04 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>How Containers Actually Work: Building Container Networking From Scratch</title><link>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/building-container-networking-from-scratch-part-1/</link><pubDate>Wed, 04 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/building-container-networking-from-scratch-part-1/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Containers often feel like magic, and container networking can seem like&#10;a higher form of black magic. A process starts, gets its own IP address,&#10;can reach the internet, and talks to other containers. All without us&#10;touching low-level networking.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But nothing magical is happening.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Under the hood, container networking is built from a small set of Linux&#10;primitives: &lt;strong&gt;network namespaces&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;virtual Ethernet devices (veth)&lt;/strong&gt;,&#10;&lt;strong&gt;routing tables&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;NAT&lt;/strong&gt;. In this write-up, we’ll build that setup&#10;manually to see exactly what Docker and other container runtimes are&#10;doing on our behalf.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>A Flood Among Trees</title><link>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/flood-amoung-trees/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/flood-amoung-trees/</guid><description>&lt;div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://amalchandran.xyz/images/flood-among-tree.jpg"&#10;style="max-width: 60%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"&#10;alt="earth-bound-misfit-i" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;A flood among trees&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>An Earth Bound Misfit, I</title><link>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/earth-bound-misfit/</link><pubDate>Mon, 19 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/earth-bound-misfit/</guid><description>&lt;div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://amalchandran.xyz/images/earth-bound-misfit-i.jpg"&#10;style="max-width: 60%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"&#10;alt="earth-bound-misfit-i" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;An earth-bound misfit, I&amp;rdquo; – Pink Floyd, &amp;ldquo;Learning to Fly&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Colors of Wes Anderson</title><link>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/wes-pallete/</link><pubDate>Thu, 27 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/wes-pallete/</guid><description>&lt;div class="container" style="text-align: left;"&gt;&#10;&lt;button id="generate-palette" onclick="generatePalette()" style="font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer; padding: 5px 8px; background-color: black; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 5px; margin-bottom: 25px"&gt;&#10; Generate Palette&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="palette" id="palette"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;p class="movie-subtext" id="movie-title"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="color-meanings"&gt;&#10;&lt;div id="color-meanings"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- Add CSS directly --&gt;&#10;&lt;style&gt;&#10; .container {&#10; max-width: 600px;&#10; }&#10; .palette {&#10; display: flex;&#10; justify-content: flex-start;&#10; margin-bottom: 30px;&#10; height: 80px;&#10; border-radius: 5px;&#10; overflow: hidden;&#10; }&#10; .color-strip {&#10; height: 100%;&#10; width: 40%;&#10; }&#10; .movie-subtext {&#10; font-size: 14px;&#10; color: #777;&#10; text-align: left;&#10; margin-top: 1px;&#10; font-style: italic;&#10; }&#10; .color-meanings {&#10; margin-top: 20px;&#10; text-align: left;&#10; }&#10; .color-meanings p {&#10; margin-bottom: 10px;&#10; font-size: 16px;&#10; color: #444;&#10; line-height: 1.5;&#10; }&#10; .color-meanings .color-swatch {&#10; width: 25px;&#10; height: 25px;&#10; margin-right: 10px;&#10; border-radius: 50%;&#10; }&#10; .color-meanings .color-name {&#10; font-weight: bold;&#10; color: #222;&#10; margin-right: 8px;&#10; }&#10; .instruction-text {&#10; font-size: 18px;&#10; color: #555;&#10; margin-top: 20px;&#10; font-weight: 500;&#10; }&#10;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- Embed JavaScript directly --&gt;&#10;&lt;script&gt;&#10;const palettes = [&#10; {&#10; movie: "Bottle Rocket",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115734/",&#10; colors: ["#ffcb6e", "#003b5c", "#f1b6a1", "#8e9aaf", "#f7f4ea"],&#10; description: "Bright pastels and offbeat suburban energy.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#ffcb6e", meaning: "Soft yellow evokes the optimistic, yet naive spirit of the film's protagonists." },&#10; { color: "#003b5c", meaning: "Deep navy speaks to the sense of ambition and the cool, calm tone of the film." },&#10; { color: "#f1b6a1", meaning: "Muted peach suggests the awkward charm and vulnerability of the characters." },&#10; { color: "#8e9aaf", meaning: "Cool blues and grays ground the film in a sense of reality amidst the absurdity." },&#10; { color: "#f7f4ea", meaning: "Warm cream adds a nostalgic, quiet softness, reflecting the film’s modest, indie vibe." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "Rushmore",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0128445/",&#10; colors: ["#d62728", "#f18f01", "#9d4a39", "#f1d7b2", "#003366"],&#10; description: "Bold reds and rich hues with schoolyard intensity.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#d62728", meaning: "Bright red captures the fiery passion and youthful energy of Max Fischer." },&#10; { color: "#f18f01", meaning: "Warm orange brings energy and optimism, despite the film's darker comedic moments." },&#10; { color: "#9d4a39", meaning: "Burnt orange and red tones suggest the emotional complexity and conflict between characters." },&#10; { color: "#f1d7b2", meaning: "Pale beige adds a softer touch, mirroring the melancholy undertones of the film." },&#10; { color: "#003366", meaning: "Dark blue anchors the film in its academic setting, providing a contrast to the chaotic energy." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "The Royal Tenenbaums",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0265666/",&#10; colors: ["#7b3f00", "#eac67a", "#d9a5b3", "#fff3e3", "#823e38"],&#10; description: "Burnt reds and dysfunctional warmth.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#7b3f00", meaning: "Deep browns evoke feelings of nostalgia, loss, and the enduring marks of family dysfunction." },&#10; { color: "#eac67a", meaning: "Golden yellows speak to faded grandeur, the warmth of family ties, and the optimism that often fades into disappointment." },&#10; { color: "#d9a5b3", meaning: "Muted pinks embody the tenderness and vulnerability hidden beneath the film's sharp humor." },&#10; { color: "#fff3e3", meaning: "Pale peach creates a sense of softness and nostalgia, the delicate residue of a once-ideal family dynamic." },&#10; { color: "#823e38", meaning: "Burnt reds reflect passion, anger, and a simmering undercurrent of unresolved emotions within the Tenenbaum family." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "The Life Aquatic with Steve Zissou",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0362270/",&#10; colors: ["#a3d2ca", "#5eaaa8", "#056676", "#f5f5f5", "#edc988"],&#10; description: "Oceanic blues and isolated brilliance.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#a3d2ca", meaning: "Soft aquamarine echoes the tranquil yet isolated nature of the ocean and the characters' inner lives." },&#10; { color: "#5eaaa8", meaning: "Teal brings an air of melancholy and introspection, marking the emotional distance of the characters from each other." },&#10; { color: "#056676", meaning: "Deep ocean blue speaks to the film’s theme of exploration and adventure, juxtaposed with personal loss." },&#10; { color: "#f5f5f5", meaning: "Cool white evokes clarity and neutrality, reflecting the sterile, sometimes detached environment of the ship." },&#10; { color: "#edc988", meaning: "Warm amber tones represent the lingering effects of passion and legacy, echoing the characters' ongoing quests." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "The Darjeeling Limited",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0838221/",&#10; colors: ["#5e2e1f", "#f3bc92", "#ce9a6a", "#7b8a6d", "#4a5561"],&#10; description: "Rich earth tones and spiritual discovery.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#5e2e1f", meaning: "Deep reds symbolize passion, conflict, and the strained relationship between the brothers." },&#10; { color: "#f3bc92", meaning: "Soft peach tones reflect the warmth and nostalgia of childhood memories and the bond of family." },&#10; { color: "#ce9a6a", meaning: "Earthy browns capture the rugged beauty of India and the characters' journey of self-discovery." },&#10; { color: "#7b8a6d", meaning: "Muted greens emphasize the spiritual calm and introspection that the film evokes." },&#10; { color: "#4a5561", meaning: "Slate grays anchor the film in its more serious, reflective moments, contrasting the vibrant surroundings." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "Fantastic Mr. Fox",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0432283/",&#10; colors: ["#ff9900", "#cc6600", "#996600", "#ffcc66", "#ffeecc"],&#10; description: "Autumnal chaos and corduroy charm.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#ff9900", meaning: "Bright orange represents the mischievous energy of Mr. Fox and his adventures, full of boldness and courage." },&#10; { color: "#cc6600", meaning: "Earthy orange tones mirror the rustic environment of the countryside, as well as the resilience of the characters." },&#10; { color: "#996600", meaning: "Deep mustard yellow suggests warmth and comfort, but also the hidden dangers of the foxes' escapades." },&#10; { color: "#ffcc66", meaning: "Light yellow adds a playful, whimsical touch to the overall aesthetic, fitting the charm and quirky tone of the story." },&#10; { color: "#ffeecc", meaning: "Soft cream shades evoke the comfort of home and family, tying into the core theme of the importance of belonging." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "Moonrise Kingdom",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt1748122/",&#10; colors: ["#f7e199", "#cdbb99", "#80775b", "#a7a8a3", "#ffecb3"],&#10; description: "Nostalgic scout-core in earthy tones.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#f7e199", meaning: "Soft yellow reflects innocence and the fleeting nature of childhood, grounding the coming-of-age narrative." },&#10; { color: "#cdbb99", meaning: "Beige tones suggest practicality and the ruggedness of a world in transition, much like the characters themselves." },&#10; { color: "#80775b", meaning: "Muted greenish browns bring a sense of earthiness and groundedness, tying the characters to nature and their desires." },&#10; { color: "#a7a8a3", meaning: "Cool grays emphasize the sense of melancholy and emotional distance, reflective of the tension in the characters’ worlds." },&#10; { color: "#ffecb3", meaning: "Soft, pastel yellow adds warmth and a touch of whimsy, fitting the adventurous and innocent spirit of the young lovers." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "The Grand Budapest Hotel",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt2278388/",&#10; colors: ["#f6c3d0", "#e9a8b2", "#9e4a64", "#fef0e3", "#5d6973"],&#10; description: "Sugary pinks and bittersweet whimsy.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#f6c3d0", meaning: "Soft pink symbolizes innocence and nostalgia, contrasting with the film’s more somber undertones." },&#10; { color: "#e9a8b2", meaning: "Muted coral evokes warmth and romanticism, tying into the themes of love and memory." },&#10; { color: "#9e4a64", meaning: "Rich burgundy mirrors the deeper emotional currents of the story, hinting at luxury and longing." },&#10; { color: "#fef0e3", meaning: "Pale yellow adds an element of lightness and hope, reminiscent of the grandeur of the hotel." },&#10; { color: "#5d6973", meaning: "Dark slate blues ground the film in sophistication and provide a cool counterpoint to the warmer tones." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "Isle of Dogs",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt5104604/",&#10; colors: ["#b9d3b8", "#e84a5f", "#1d1f2c", "#f4bfa5", "#c0a8a1"],&#10; description: "Muted tones with stark contrasts and loyalty.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#b9d3b8", meaning: "Soft greens represent the lushness of the island and the enduring bond between the dogs." },&#10; { color: "#e84a5f", meaning: "Vivid red evokes the urgency and emotional intensity of the film’s themes of loyalty and sacrifice." },&#10; { color: "#1d1f2c", meaning: "Deep blues and blacks add a serious, industrial tone, emphasizing the dystopian setting." },&#10; { color: "#f4bfa5", meaning: "Warm peaches contrast the bleakness of the story, adding a layer of humor and humanity to the struggle." },&#10; { color: "#c0a8a1", meaning: "Muted grays represent the film’s melancholic reflections and the isolation of the dogs." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "The French Dispatch",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt8847712/",&#10; colors: ["#e9d5b6", "#6f4f4f", "#d34e2e", "#a0a9b6", "#efc8c2"],&#10; description: "Crisp colors with a vintage, editorial feel.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#e9d5b6", meaning: "Pale beige suggests nostalgia and the timeless quality of journalistic storytelling." },&#10; { color: "#6f4f4f", meaning: "Warm browns reflect the earthiness of the film's setting and the enduring nature of print media." },&#10; { color: "#d34e2e", meaning: "Vibrant red brings an intensity to the story’s exploration of art, activism, and personal passion." },&#10; { color: "#a0a9b6", meaning: "Cool blues add a professional, polished air, fitting the refined aesthetic of the magazine." },&#10; { color: "#efc8c2", meaning: "Soft pinks highlight the tenderness and eccentricity of the film’s characters and their stories." }&#10; ]&#10; },&#10; {&#10; movie: "Asteroid City",&#10; imdb: "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt14230388/",&#10; colors: ["#e4b7a0", "#9abdb2", "#3c4f66", "#e7e5b4", "#af5b40"],&#10; description: "Retro pastels with a cosmic flair.",&#10; colorMeanings: [&#10; { color: "#e4b7a0", meaning: "Peach tones evoke a sense of nostalgia and softness, countering the film’s existential themes." },&#10; { color: "#9abdb2", meaning: "Muted teal represents the tension between the futuristic setting and timeless human emotions." },&#10; { color: "#3c4f66", meaning: "Dark blues and grays anchor the cosmic setting, reflecting the isolation and vastness of space." },&#10; { color: "#e7e5b4", meaning: "Pale yellows and greens bring a touch of surrealism, hinting at the strange, dream-like qualities of the film." },&#10; { color: "#af5b40", meaning: "Earthy browns suggest the human connection to the environment and the film's existential reflections." }&#10; ]&#10; }&#10;];&#10; function generatePalette() {&#10; const palette = palettes[Math.floor(Math.random() * palettes.length)];&#10; const paletteDiv = document.getElementById("palette");&#10; paletteDiv.innerHTML = "";&#10; // Generate the palette with stripes of colors&#10; const paletteWidth = palette.colors.length * 100;&#10; palette.colors.forEach((color, index) =&gt; {&#10; const stripe = document.createElement("div");&#10; stripe.className = "color-stripe";&#10; stripe.style.backgroundColor = color;&#10; stripe.style.width = `${100}%`;&#10; stripe.style.height = "100%";&#10; paletteDiv.appendChild(stripe);&#10; });&#10; // Update movie title and description as a single subtext under the palette&#10;document.getElementById("movie-title").innerHTML = `&lt;a href="${palette.imdb}" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;${palette.movie}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: ${palette.description}`;&#10; const colorMeaningsDiv = document.getElementById("color-meanings");&#10; colorMeaningsDiv.innerHTML = "";&#10; palette.colorMeanings.forEach(meaning =&gt; {&#10; const p = document.createElement("p");&#10; p.innerHTML = `&lt;strong style="color:${meaning.color}"&gt;${meaning.color}&lt;/strong&gt;: ${meaning.meaning}`;&#10; colorMeaningsDiv.appendChild(p);&#10; });&#10; }&#10;&lt;/script&gt;</description></item><item><title>The Caged Song</title><link>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/creativity/</link><pubDate>Sat, 22 Feb 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/creativity/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I used to believe that creativity thrived in absolute freedom.&lt;br&gt;&#10;But over time, I wondered, do limits hold it back, or do they give it&#10;shape?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A bird in flight may roam the skies,&lt;br&gt;&#10;Yet sings no tune, just silent sighs.&lt;br&gt;&#10;But cage the wings, confine its space,&lt;br&gt;&#10;A melody will fill the place.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;For freedom vast may lose its way,&lt;br&gt;&#10;While boundaries teach the notes to play.&lt;br&gt;&#10;Not every wall is built to bind,&lt;br&gt;&#10;Some shape the song within the mind.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>2024 -&gt; 2025</title><link>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/blogpost/</link><pubDate>Tue, 31 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://amalchandran.xyz/journals/blogpost/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;2024 was a busy year. I shifted two houses this year, visited four&#10;places on my travel list, completed two half marathons, and went on a&#10;long bike trip of 650+ kilometers. I also found myself in some tough&#10;conversations and situations.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here are some lessons I learned this year. Some are common sense, but&#10;I’ve included them because I tend to overlook the obvious. Some are my&#10;own realizations, and others come from wise people I’ve met along the&#10;way:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>